  "placeholders": [
    {
      "path": "System/Repositories/TruvioCommerce/Products.index",
      "kind": "repository",
      "why": "The storefront product index this distribution owns, so the facet set matches the catalogue it ships instead of the host design package's stock one."
    },
    {
      "path": "System/Repositories/TruvioCommerce/Products.query",
      "kind": "repository",
      "why": "The query the Shop paragraph binds. Carries the full Swift parameter set, so no surface that passes a parameter silently filters to nothing."
    },
    {
      "path": "System/Repositories/TruvioCommerce/Products.facets",
      "kind": "repository",
      "why": "Three base-schema facets and a commented recipe for a category-field and a Range facet. A facet bound to a field with no values renders and filters nothing."
    },
    {
      "path": "System/Items/ItemType_TC_AnchorNav.xml",
      "kind": "itemtype",
      "why": "An in-page jump strip as a real item type, so a site does not author one as raw markup inside a Text paragraph. Rendered by Templates/Designs/Swift-v2/Paragraph/TC_AnchorNav.cshtml, which ships beside it; the strip is inert on any page that does not carry the paragraph."
    },
    {
      "path": "System/Items/ItemType_TC_AnchorNav_Item.xml",
      "kind": "itemtype",
      "why": "The repeater child of TC_AnchorNav: label plus anchor id, no defaults, so a missing field renders visibly empty."
    },
    {
      "path": "Templates/Designs/Swift-v2/Paragraph/TC_AnchorNav.cshtml",
      "kind": "template",
      "why": "The renderer for TC_AnchorNav. Emits its shell even with no links, so the section is measurable when the repeater is empty; the theme's default_custom.js fills an empty strip from the page's own main h2[id] headings and repoints every href past Dynamicweb's sitewide <base href>."
    },
    {
      "path": "Templates/Designs/Swift-v2/Paragraph/Swift-v2_ProductMedia.cshtml",
      "kind": "template",
      "why": "The PDP hero gallery. A one-token override of the stock Swift 2.4 render path: \".svg\" added to the supportedImageFormats allowlist, and nothing else. Stock ProductMedia resolves images by asset-category system name (which matched all along) and then discards every asset whose path does not contain one of seven hardcoded raster extensions, so an SVG catalogue renders a carousel with no slides in it while the PLP card, which applies no format filter, renders the same rows. Inert on a raster catalogue: identical output to stock."
    },
    {
      "path": "Templates/Designs/Swift-v2/eCom/ProductCatalog/RelatedProductsList.cshtml",
      "kind": "template",
      "why": "A data-leak fix, and the one file in this layer that overrides a stock render path by name rather than waiting to be named by a paragraph. Swift 2.4 ships this list with no read of the area's AnonymousUsers gate, so a PDP whose price column shows the sign-in lock still serves every related product's price in the same HTML - itemprop=price, itemprop=priceCurrency, and a third copy in the cart form's hidden ProductPrice input. The override adds the two booleans the stock file already has the ingredients for and suppresses the two cells' contents, keeping both <td> so the header row still lines up. Inert on any area that does not gate prices."
    }
  ]
}
